# Bokklubben – Cursor Rules

## Project
Multi-tenant book club platform. Next.js 15 App Router, Supabase (Postgres), Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui.

## Auth Model
No user accounts. Per-group **group password** (always use this phrase). JWT stored in localStorage as `bookclub_[slug]_token`. Verified server-side on every protected API route. Never call this "password" alone — always "group password".

## Code Rules
- TypeScript strict — no `any`
- No client-side Supabase writes — all mutations go through API Route Handlers using `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`
- Tailwind only — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- shadcn/ui for all interactive components
- File names: `kebab-case`. Component names: `PascalCase`
- Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only when needed
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix only for values safe to expose to the browser

## Naming
- `groups` — group table; `slug` is the URL identifier
- `group_books` — join table linking groups to books with a status (`want_to_read` | `already_read`)
- `books` — shared catalog, keyed by `google_books_id`
- `ratings` — per group-book, per `rater_id` (anonymous UUID from localStorage); scale 1–10

## Routes
- `/` — landing
- `/[slug]` — group page
- `/[slug]/settings` — admin (group password required)
- `/[slug]/books/[bookId]` — book detail

## Environment Variables
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` — public
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY`, `JWT_SECRET`, `GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY` — server only, never expose
